 # Tetrahedral representation and traversal
 
-Also called: Projected Tetrahedra, Cell Projection with Tetrahedra
+Also called: Projected Tetrahedra, Tetrahedral Volume Rendering, Marching Tetrahedrons, Adaptive Delaunay Update, Grid-based Traversal, Parallel Projected Tetrahedra, Tetrahedral Mesh Connectivity Encoding
 
 ## Overview
-Tetrahedral representation and traversal is a family of object-order volume rendering techniques that decompose volumetric data into tetrahedral cells, project them onto the 2D image plane, and rasterize the resulting polygons to leverage hardware-accelerated graphics pipelines [S1, S2, S4, S6, S7, S8, S9, S10, S11, S12, S14, S16, S17, S18]. It solves the problem of efficiently rendering unstructured tetrahedral grids by converting 3D geometric primitives into 2D fragments that can be composited in back-to-front order [S1, S2, S4, S6, S8, S9, S10, S11, S12, S14, S16, S17, S18]. Unlike [Tetrahedral Volume Rendering](820-tetrahedral-volume-rendering.md), which typically relies on ray casting, this family uses explicit geometric projection and scan-conversion [S2, S4, S6, S7, S12, S14, S16]. It differs from [GPU-based Projected Tetrahedra](7484-gpu-based-projected-tetrahedra.md) in that the core algorithm performs sorting and projection in software, whereas later variants offload these steps to the GPU [S4, S7, S12, S14, S16].
+Tetrahedral representation and traversal decomposes volumetric data into tetrahedral cells to leverage their geometric simplicity for rendering, isosurface extraction, or spatial acceleration. Unlike hexahedral methods that may suffer from topological ambiguities or require complex connectivity handling, tetrahedra provide a consistent, convex primitive that simplifies intersection tests and sorting [S1, unofficial][S2][S4, S6, S7][S8, S9, S10, unofficial][S11][S12, unofficial][S14, S16][S17, S18, unofficial]. This family encompasses explicit geometric projection for volume rendering [877-projected-tetrahedra.md], topological isosurface extraction [940-marching-tetrahedrons-algorithm.md], and spatial traversal structures for ray tracing [7083-grid-based-traversal.md].
 
